{
 "_bob": {
  "id": "mesh_geom_mv",
  "plan": "W6, docs/COMFYUI.md family 2 (track C), the multi-view geometry challenger",
  "purpose": "Four views of a subject to a watertight mesh, for when a single view guesses the back wrong. Views come from Blender when a block-out exists, so they are consistent by construction rather than by luck.",
  "derived_from": "comfyui_workflow_templates_json/templates/3d_hunyuan3d_multiview_to_model.json, converted by tools/scripts/comfy_ui_to_api.py",
  "deviations_from_source": [
   "BOB_* titles added on the templated nodes. BOB_3D_MODEL is meaningful here for the same reason it is in W5: ImageOnlyCheckpointLoader does name a checkpoint file.",
   "SaveGLB's filename_prefix moved from mesh/ComfyUI to bob_mesh, matching W5, so a Bob run is identifiable in the output folder.",
   "MarkdownNote nodes dropped; they are GUI documentation.",
   "Nothing else. Latent 3072, 20 steps, cfg 7.5, euler + normal are the template's own multi-view values."
  ],
  "requires_nodes": [
   "ImageOnlyCheckpointLoader",
   "Hunyuan3Dv2ConditioningMultiView",
   "VAEDecodeHunyuan3D",
   "VoxelToMesh",
   "SaveGLB"
  ],
  "requires_pack": "none, all five are ComfyUI core",
  "runtime_inputs": [
   "BOB_VIEW_FRONT.image",
   "BOB_VIEW_LEFT.image",
   "BOB_VIEW_BACK.image",
   "BOB_VIEW_RIGHT.image"
  ],
  "notes": "CLIPVisionEncode crop is 'none' here, not 'center' as in W5: cropping four views independently would centre each one differently and the four would stop describing one object. That is the template's own choice and it is load-bearing. The four views are the four cardinal angles at the same elevation, in the order front, left, back, right, which is the order Hunyuan3Dv2ConditioningMultiView's sockets name. Output is watertight SDF-voxel geometry, so this graph structurally cannot make a leaf; it is the hard-surface and back-facing route. Swap BOB_3D_MODEL to hunyuan3d-dit-v2-mv-turbo_fp16 with cfg 4 for the turbo variant, which additionally needs a FluxGuidance node."
 },
